-- tools/ci/serial-tests.conf.mix: test binaries tools/ci/test_pool.mix runs
-- alone, after the parallel pool, because they measure wall-clock time or
-- look at the whole machine and so fail when other tests run beside them.
--
-- Strict data. Each entry names the cargo package and test target and says
-- why, with the evidence. The list only shrinks: fix the test (scope it to
-- its own process group, time a CPU budget instead of wall clock) and
-- delete its entry in the same PR.

serial_tests: [
  {
    package: "mix",
    target: "native_session_pty",
    reason: "p4 tests assert pgrep -f 'sleep 600' finds nothing on the whole machine (tests/native_session_pty.rs:3317, :3378); PTY timing; red when another job runs the suite (2026-11-12)"
  },
  {
    package: "lib-viu",
    target: "backdrop",
    reason: "backdrop_colours_modes_outputs_and_refusals_use_mix reads app.model right after the reply, so a model update that lands after it shows the previous mode (left fit, right centre, tests/backdrop.rs:239); 4 failures sequentially on 2026-11-07, 1 in the pool on a loaded cbc2 (2026-11-13). Make the test wait for the model of its own request, then delete this entry"
  },
  {
    package: "portald",
    target: "portal",
    reason: "native_recovers_when_broker_returns_after_the_initial_attempt_budget and native_startup_live_change_and_settingsd_restart_without_broker_reconnect hit their deadline under load (cbc3 2026-11-12 without the pool; the pool on a loaded cbc2, 2026-11-13). Give the deadlines a measured margin or wait on observable state, then delete this entry"
  },
  {
    package: "mix",
    target: "exec_stdio_routing",
    reason: "abandoned_in_flight_stream_write_cannot_follow_return is timing-sensitive: red on main's own hosted run at 4e69abbc (2026-11-12), where binaries already ran one at a time, so running it alone does not cure it; it is kept out of the pool so the extra load does not make it worse. Fix the test, then delete this entry"
  }
]
